{
 "duration": 52.0,
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.2,
   "text": "Everyone warns you about generators.",
   "end": 2.66
  },
  {
   "start": 2.66,
   "text": "But in the twenty twenty one Texas freeze, the cold took the most lives.",
   "end": 7.16
  },
  {
   "start": 7.16,
   "text": "So who were they?",
   "end": 8.5
  },
  {
   "start": 8.5,
   "text": "The state confirmed one hundred fifty eight hypothermia deaths.",
   "end": 12.54
  },
  {
   "start": 12.54,
   "text": "One hundred seven of them, more than two out of three, were sixty or older.",
   "end": 17.16
  },
  {
   "start": 17.16,
   "text": "One storm, confirmed deaths only.",
   "end": 19.38
  },
  {
   "start": 19.38,
   "text": "If someone you love is over sixty, this is about them.",
   "end": 22.83
  },
  {
   "start": 22.83,
   "text": "So what do you do?",
   "end": 24.23
  },
  {
   "start": 24.23,
   "text": "The CDC says check on older friends and neighbors often, and make sure their homes are heated properly.",
   "end": 30.66
  },
  {
   "start": 30.66,
   "text": "Call them before the storm hits, while phones still work.",
   "end": 34.29
  },
  {
   "start": 34.29,
   "text": "We're not doctors.",
   "end": 35.69
  },
  {
   "start": 35.69,
   "text": "Per the CDC, a body temperature below ninety five degrees is an emergency.",
   "end": 40.42
  },
  {
   "start": 40.42,
   "text": "Get medical help right away.",
   "end": 42.41
  },
  {
   "start": 42.41,
   "text": "What took the other eighty five people is in the full video, linked below.",
   "end": 47.03
  },
  {
   "start": 47.03,
   "text": "What's the longest you've ever gone without heat?",
   "end": 50.25
  },
  {
   "start": 50.25,
   "text": "Tell us in the comments.",
   "end": 52.0
  }
 ],
